### C-02: `.env.production` Contains Stale Placeholder Values — Will Crash Build

| Field | Detail |
|-------|--------|
| **File** | `apps/web/.env.production` |
| **Impact** | If Vercel reads this file, it overrides real env vars with `xxx` placeholders |

**Root Cause:** The `.env.production` file contains entries like:
```
NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL=https://your-domain.com
NEXT_PUBLIC_STRIPE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=pk_live_xxx
NEXT_PUBLIC_SENTRY_DSN=https://xxx@xxx.ingest.sentry.io/xxx
```

This file also references **Stripe** (`NEXT_PUBLIC_STRIPE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY`) which is NOT used in the codebase — the platform uses **Razorpay**. It references `NEXT_PUBLIC_GA_ID`, `NEXT_PUBLIC_HOTJAR_ID`, `NEXT_PUBLIC_MIXPANEL_TOKEN`, `NEXT_PUBLIC_CLOUDFRONT_DOMAIN` — none of which exist in any source file.

**Risk:** Vercel loads `.env.production` during `NODE_ENV=production` builds. If Vercel env vars are not set to override these, the Algolia client initializes with `APP_ID='xxx'` and will throw on every search request.

**Fix:** Delete `.env.production` entirely (env vars should be managed exclusively via Vercel dashboard). Also delete `.env.local` and `.env` from the repo (they are committed and contain secrets).

