### C-05: `validate` Route Has Its Own `connectDB()` — Bypasses Connection Pooling

| Field | Detail |
|-------|--------|
| **File** | [src/app/api/deals/[id]/validate/route.ts](file:///e:/Awesome%20Projects/ShadowMerchant/apps/web/src/app/api/deals/%5Bid%5D/validate/route.ts) (lines 21-26) |
| **Impact** | Connection leak, potential MongoDB "topology destroyed" errors under load |

**Root Cause:** The validate route defines its own `connectDB()` function instead of importing from `@/lib/db`:
```ts
async function connectDB() {
  if (mongoose.connection.readyState === 0) {
    if (!MONGODB_URI) throw new Error('MONGODB_URI not defined');
    await mongoose.connect(MONGODB_URI);
  }
}
```
This bypasses the global connection cache, the `dbName: 'shadowmerchant'` setting, and all timeout/pool config from the shared module. Under concurrent requests, this creates orphan connections.

**Fix:** Replace with `import { connectDB } from '@/lib/db';` and delete the local function.

