## 🟠 HIGH — Runtime Errors & Data Integrity (P1)

### H-01: `tatacliq` In Schema Enum But Missing From `PLATFORM_CONFIG`

| Field | Detail |
|-------|--------|
| **Files** | [models/Deal.ts](file:///e:/Awesome%20Projects/ShadowMerchant/apps/web/src/models/Deal.ts#L36) enum, [lib/platforms.ts](file:///e:/Awesome%20Projects/ShadowMerchant/apps/web/src/lib/platforms.ts), [types/index.ts](file:///e:/Awesome%20Projects/ShadowMerchant/apps/web/src/types/index.ts#L6) |
| **Impact** | TataCliq deals render with fallback config (missing `tier` field → `getPlatform` returns object without `tier`) |

The Deal schema enum includes `'tatacliq'`, the types include `'tatacliq'`, the homepage mentions "TataCliq", and `next.config.ts` has image domains for `img.tatacliq.com` — but `PLATFORM_CONFIG` in `platforms.ts` has no `tatacliq` entry. The `getPlatform()` fallback returns an object **without the `tier` property**, which means `platform.tier === 'value'` checks in DealCard will work (they're just undefined/falsy), but the platform won't have proper colors or branding.

**Fix:** Add a `tatacliq` entry to `PLATFORM_CONFIG`.

