### H-02: `reactions_cache` Type Mismatch Between Model and TypeScript Interface

| Field | Detail |
|-------|--------|
| **Files** | [models/Deal.ts](file:///e:/Awesome%20Projects/ShadowMerchant/apps/web/src/models/Deal.ts#L89-L93) vs [types/index.ts](file:///e:/Awesome%20Projects/ShadowMerchant/apps/web/src/types/index.ts#L45) |
| **Impact** | TypeScript lies about the data shape; `reactions_cache.love` doesn't exist in DB |

The Mongoose schema defines: `{ fire, meh, expired }`  
The TypeScript type defines: `{ fire?, love?, meh? }` — note `love` instead of `expired`.

DealCard uses `(deal as any).reactions_cache` to bypass the type system, which masks this bug. But any component relying on the TypeScript `Deal` type for reaction rendering will silently fail to show `expired` counts and show non-existent `love` counts.

**Fix:** Align the TypeScript interface to `{ fire?: number; meh?: number; expired?: number }`.

