### H-06: `clerkClient` Import Style Differs Between Payment Webhook and Cron Route

| Field | Detail |
|-------|--------|
| **Files** | [payments/webhook/route.ts](file:///e:/Awesome%20Projects/ShadowMerchant/apps/web/src/app/api/payments/webhook/route.ts#L5) (top-level import) vs [cron/refresh-deals/route.ts](file:///e:/Awesome%20Projects/ShadowMerchant/apps/web/src/app/api/cron/refresh-deals/route.ts#L34) (dynamic import) |
| **Impact** | Potential crash in payment webhook route |

The payment webhook does:
```ts
import { clerkClient } from '@clerk/nextjs/server';
// ...
const clerk = await clerkClient();
```

But in `@clerk/nextjs` v7, `clerkClient` is an async factory function. The top-level import works, but the webhook route depends on this being resolved at module load time during the Vercel serverless cold start. The cron route correctly uses a dynamic `import()` inside the handler. Both patterns technically work, but the static import forces Clerk SDK initialization on every cold start of the webhook route, even for non-subscription events.

**Fix:** Standardize to dynamic import pattern for consistency and cold-start performance.

