## 🟡 MEDIUM — Functional Bugs & Data Issues (P2)

### M-01: Homepage `generateMetadata` Calls `getDealDetails` Twice (Double View Count)

| Field | Detail |
|-------|--------|
| **File** | [deals/[id]/page.tsx](file:///e:/Awesome%20Projects/ShadowMerchant/apps/web/src/app/%28public%29/deals/%5Bid%5D/page.tsx) |
| **Impact** | Every deal page load increments `view_count` by 2 |

`generateMetadata()` at line 48 calls `getDealDetails(id)` which does `findByIdAndUpdate($inc: view_count)`. Then the page component at line 86 calls `getDealDetails(id)` again. Next.js de-duplicates `fetch()` calls but NOT direct MongoDB queries. Each page load increments `view_count` by 2.

**Fix:** Split into a read-only metadata fetcher (no `$inc`) and a separate view-tracking call.

