### M-04: Redis Cache Never Invalidated For Deal-Specific Keys

| Field | Detail |
|-------|--------|
| **Files** | [cron/refresh-deals/route.ts](file:///e:/Awesome%20Projects/ShadowMerchant/apps/web/src/app/api/cron/refresh-deals/route.ts#L46-L64), [lib/redis.ts](file:///e:/Awesome%20Projects/ShadowMerchant/apps/web/src/lib/redis.ts#L50) |
| **Impact** | Individual deal cache (`deal:<id>`) and per-filter list caches survive cron refresh |

The refresh cron clears specific known cache keys, but never clears:
- Individual deal caches: `deal:<id>` (15-min TTL)
- Arbitrary filter combinations: `deals:<querystring>` (5-min TTL)
- The feed cache: `deals:feed:<JSON>` (5-min TTL)

The TTLs are short enough that this is unlikely to cause visible issues, but stale data can persist for up to 15 minutes after a scraper run completes.

**Fix:** Add a wildcard key scan or use a versioned cache prefix that increments on each cron run.

